## Premise

You are a survivor who washed ashore on **Hollow Shore** — a strange, living wilderness with no memory of how you arrived. Scattered across the land are six ancient **Sanctums**, each guarded by a powerful boss and hiding a piece of the **Tide Portal** that will carry you home. To survive long enough to find them all, you'll need to build, farm, craft, hunt, fish, and fight your way across an ever-darkening world.

---

## World Structure & Map System

### 9-Section Grid

The world is divided into a **3×3 grid of nine large sections**. The player spawns in the center section (Section 5). Each section is **160×160 tiles**, giving roughly 10+ screens of exploration space per section and a total world of 480×480 tiles — large by GBA standards.

Sections load individually. When the player reaches the edge of their current section, a brief fade-to-black transition loads the adjacent section. Only one section is active in memory at a time. Timers for crops, resource respawns, and monster escalation continue ticking based on total in-game days elapsed, even while a section is unloaded.

```
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
|   SECTION 1      |   SECTION 2      |   SECTION 3      |
|   [TUNDRA]       |   [HIGHLANDS]    |   [VOLCANIC]     |
|                  |                  |                  |
|  * Frostspire    |  * Bear Country  |  * Emberdepth    |
|    (Sanctum 3)   |    (Rare Threat) |    (Sanctum 5)   |
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
|   SECTION 4      |   SECTION 5      |   SECTION 6      |
|   [COASTAL]      |   [FOREST HUB]   |   [MARSHLAND]    |
|                  |                  |                  |
|  * Tidecrypt     |  *** SPAWN ***   |  * Marshveil     |
|    (Sanctum 2)   |    Safe Zone     |    (Sanctum 4)   |
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
|   SECTION 7      |   SECTION 8      |   SECTION 9      |
|   [DEEP FOREST]  |   [COASTAL]      |   [CORRUPTED]    |
|                  |                  |                  |
|  * Roothold      |  * Fishing Cove  |  * Hollow Throne |
|    (Sanctum 1)   |    (Rich Fish)   |    (Sanctum 6)   |
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
```

### Section Transition Rules

- Transitions trigger only at section edges — the player must deliberately walk there
- Visual cues mark boundaries: thinning treelines, river crossings, mountain passes, fog banks
- Each section saves its state independently: tile changes, placed structures, crop stages, chest contents, boss defeat flags
- Only one section is held in VRAM at a time — clean memory management for GBA hardware
- The center section (Section 5) is always the safest — gentle resources, closest to spawn
- The Hollow Throne (Section 9) is diagonally opposite spawn — maximum distance, maximum tension

### Section 5 — The Spawn Zone

The center section is the player's home base. It features a neutral forest clearing with visible basic resources nearby. It has no Sanctum. Monster spawns here are always one tier below the current world escalation level, making it a reliable safe haven to return to. The player's first bed and first structures will almost always be built here.

