## Core Systems

### Day / Night Cycle

- 24 in-game hours per full cycle — approximately 1 real minute per in-game hour (24 min full day)
- **Dawn (6AM):** Monsters retreat, animals appear, crops tick forward
- **Day (6AM–8PM):** Safe exploration, farming, building, fishing
- **Dusk (8PM):** Lighting becomes critical, monsters begin spawning at map edges
- **Night (8PM–6AM):** Monsters fully active, Bear can roam after Day 5+
- Sky color shifts gradually signal transitions — no clock on the HUD, player reads the sky
- Weather is telegraphed the evening before by sky color and ambient wind sounds

---

### Stamina System

- Stamina bar displayed beneath the health bar
- Depleted by: sprinting (hold B), chopping trees, mining rocks, heavy combat swings
- Regenerates slowly when standing still, faster when resting near a bed
- Low stamina: tool swing speed reduces, sprint becomes unavailable
- Food restores stamina alongside hunger — core incentive for cooking over raw eating
- Craftable **Herb Pouch** (accessory slot) increases max stamina pool

---

### Hunger System

- Hunger drains over time, faster during stamina-heavy activity
- Stages: **Full → Satisfied → Hungry → Starving**
- Starving: health drains slowly, stamina does not regenerate
- Raw food gives minimal hunger value and risks a mild debuff (slowed stamina regen)
- Cooked food gives full hunger value plus temporary stat buffs

| Meal | Ingredients | Buff |
|---|---|---|
| Roast Meat | Meat + Fire | +Stamina regeneration rate |
| Fish Stew | Fish + Herb + Water | +Max stamina temporarily |
| Vegetable Soup | 2x Crop + Water | +Health regeneration |
| Hunter's Feast | Meat + Crop + Herb | All stats briefly boosted |
| Grilled Catch | Fish + Fire | Quick hunger fill, no buff |

---

### Inventory System

- Base capacity: **16 slots**
- Hotbar: **8 slots** visible at screen bottom, cycled with L/R triggers
- **Upgrades:**
  - Small Backpack (10 Leather + 5 Wood) → +8 slots
  - Large Backpack (20 Leather + Iron Buckle) → +16 slots
  - Explorer's Pack (rare depth materials) → +24 slots + map pocket
- Auto-sort: Select + A in inventory screen
- Items stack where logical: materials, seeds, food
- Tab categories: **All / Tools / Materials / Food / Seeds / Equipment**

---

### Resource Gathering

| Resource | Tool | Yields |
|---|---|---|
| Trees | Axe | Wood, Branches, Rare Sap |
| Rocks | Pickaxe | Stone, Flint, Ore |
| Grass / Soil | Shovel | Dirt, Clay, Seeds (random) |
| Water tiles | Fishing Rod | Fish, Kelp, Treasure (rare) |
| Bushes | Hands / Axe | Berries, Fiber, Twigs |
| Deer / Rabbit | Bow / Sword | Meat, Leather, Bone |
| Bear (rare) | Best weapons | Premium Leather, Bear Meat |

- Resource nodes respawn after **3 in-game days**
- Deeper / harsher biomes yield better materials — volcanic rock gives Iron Ore, tundra gives Crystal Shards
- Rare resource variants glow faintly to distinguish them on the GBA screen

---

### Crafting System

- Recipes **auto-unlock** when a new material is first picked up — no recipe hunting
- Crafting stations required for advanced items:

| Station | Unlocks |
|---|---|
| Hands (default) | Basic tools, campfire, rope, simple furniture |
| Workbench | Furniture, backpacks, weapons, doors, fencing |
| Forge | Metal tools, armor, metal building materials |
| Cooking Fire / Stove | All meals and food items |
| Alchemy Table | Potions, depth gear, portal components |

---

### Building System

- All structures placed on the tile grid
- **Place mode:** select item from hotbar, press A on target tile
- **Break mode:** hold B on a placed structure to recover partial materials
- **Upgrade in-place:** stand next to a wall, hold A with higher tier material

**Wall Tiers:**

| Tier | Material | Monster Resistance |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Wood | Low — goblins breach in 3–4 hits |
| 2 | Stone | Medium — requires sustained attack |
| 3 | Brick | High — only late-game enemies breach |
| 4 | Metal | Very High — effectively siege-proof |

**Lighting as Defense:**
- Torches, lanterns, and braziers prevent monster spawning within their light radius
- Monsters avoid lit areas unless actively chasing the player
- Light sources consume fuel over time — Wood (torch), Oil (lantern), Coal (brazier)
- Wraiths and late-game enemies ignore light — endgame escalation threat

**Flooring Types:**

| Flooring | Category | Removed With |
|---|---|---|
| Wood Plank | Indoor | Shovel — returns partial wood |
| Stone Tile | Indoor | Shovel — returns partial stone |
| Wool Rug | Indoor | Hands — full return |
| Gravel Path | Outdoor | Shovel — returns gravel |
| Cobblestone | Outdoor | Shovel — returns partial stone |
| Dirt Track | Outdoor | Shovel — no return |

---

### Farming System

- Till soil with shovel on grass tiles → plant seeds → water daily → harvest after growth period
- **Seasons** cycle every 7 in-game days:
  - **Spring:** All crops grow normally
  - **Summer:** Fast-growing crops, drought risk without daily watering
  - **Autumn:** Root vegetables and grain thrive
  - **Winter:** Only cold-resistant herbs survive without a Greenhouse structure
- Crops die if unwatered 2 consecutive days
- **Fence** protects crops from deer, rabbits, and slows monster pathing
- **Scarecrow** (5 Wood + 5 Fiber) deters animals without requiring full fencing
- High-tier meals require multiple crop types grown across several seasons — rewards long-term players

---

### Weather System

Weather changes every 1–3 in-game days and is telegraphed the evening before by sky color and ambient wind sounds.

| Weather | Effect |
|---|---|
| Rain | Auto-waters crops, slows player movement slightly, reduces night monster spawn rate |
| Clear / Sunny | Crops dry faster, require manual watering or risk wilting |
| Storm | Heavy rain, no monster spawns, structures take minor chip damage if untended |
| Blizzard (Winter) | Heavy movement penalty outdoors, hunger drains faster, fires extinguish |

---

### Combat System

**Weapons:**

| Weapon | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Sword | Melee | Fast, short range, reliable |
| Axe | Melee | Slower, higher damage, doubles as tree-chopping tool |
| Bow + Arrow | Ranged | Arrows consumed on use, crafted from Wood + Feather |
| Spear | Mid-range | Pierces through multiple enemies in a line |

**Armor Tiers:**

| Tier | Material | Defense |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Leather | Basic — crafted from hunted animals |
| 2 | Chain | Medium — Iron Rings at the Forge |
| 3 | Iron | High — full Iron Ore processing |
| 4 | Sanctum Alloy | Best — boss drops only |

---

### Monster Escalation

- **Days 1–3:** Slimes, bats — low HP, no aggression at range, tutorial-level threats
- **Days 4–7:** Wolves, goblins — chase player, begin attacking base structures
- **Days 8–15:** Armored goblins, wraiths — wraiths ignore light, require weapons above a damage threshold
- **Day 15+:** Siege events every 3rd night — coordinated monster waves target your base
- **Bear:** Spawns randomly in northern sections after Day 5, patrols a territory, rare premium drops
- Section 5 (spawn) always runs one tier below the current world escalation level

