## The Six Sanctums

Six ancient Sanctums are placed at the outer sections of the 3×3 grid, forming a wide circle around the player's spawn. Each is marked by a **visible landmark** from a distance — no quest markers, discovery is organic. Each contains a 3-floor dungeon, a boss, and a Portal Piece.

| Sanctum | Section | Biome | Difficulty | Recommended Gear |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 — The Roothold | 7 (SW) | Deep Forest | ★☆☆☆☆ | Basic Wood/Stone tools, Leather armor |
| 2 — The Tidecrypt | 4 (W) | Coastal Shore | ★★☆☆☆ | Stone tools, Leather/Chain armor, Bow |
| 3 — The Frostspire | 1 (NW) | Tundra | ★★★☆☆ | Iron tools, Chain armor, food buffs stocked |
| 4 — The Marshveil | 6 (E) | Marshland | ★★★☆☆ | Iron tools, anti-poison potions, Spear |
| 5 — The Emberdepth | 3 (NE) | Volcanic | ★★★★☆ | Full Iron/Sanctum armor, fire resistance potion |
| 6 — The Hollow Throne | 9 (SE) | Corrupted | ★★★★★ | All 5 Portal Pieces + best available gear |

---

### Sanctum 1 — The Roothold *(Deep Forest, SW)*

Ancient overgrown ruins buried in the deep forest. Designed as the player's first dungeon — teaches dungeon mechanics gently. **Landmark:** a massive moss-covered stone arch visible through the treeline.

- **Floor 1 — Puzzle introduction:** Pressure plates open doors, spike tile hazards teach floor awareness
- **Floor 2 — Ambush rooms:** Enemies hidden in breakable pots and crates, introduces chest looting
- **Floor 3 — Boss: The Root Warden**
  - A massive animated tree creature with a glowing core
  - **Attacks:** Ground slam shockwave lines, spawns Vine Whips on flanks, briefly roots the player
  - **Strategy:** Destroy Vine Whips first to stop constant chip damage, strike the core during arm recovery
  - **Drop:** Verdant Shard (Portal Piece 1) + Bark Steel (mid-tier armor crafting material)

---

### Sanctum 2 — The Tidecrypt *(Coastal Shore, W)*

A half-sunken ruin emerging from the ocean cliffs. Tidal water floods the lower floors on a timer. **Landmark:** a glowing stone spire jutting from the sea cliff, visible from the coastal section.

- **Floor 1 — Tidal mechanics:** Water rises and falls on a timer, some floors only passable at low tide
- **Floor 2 — Flooded corridors:** Swimmer enemies, air pocket navigation to avoid a drowning timer
- **Floor 3 — Boss: The Drowned Warden**
  - A massive coral-armored sea creature rising from a flooded chamber
  - **Attacks:** Tidal wave sweeps the room pushing player into walls, spawns Tide Crawlers, ranged spits
  - **Strategy:** Move perpendicular to avoid the wave, attack exposed underbelly after each sweep
  - **Drop:** Tide Shard (Portal Piece 2) + Coralite (water-resistant armor coating material)

---

### Sanctum 3 — The Frostspire *(Tundra, NW)*

A tall frozen tower jutting from the snowfield. Floors **ascend** rather than descend — the player climbs rather than digs. **Landmark:** the spire is visible from nearly any point in the tundra section.

- **Floor 1 — Ice mechanics:** Slippery floor tiles create momentum sliding, enemies exploit this too
- **Floor 2 — Frozen enemies:** Encased in ice blocks, usable as cover or breakable for loot
- **Floor 3 — Boss: The Glacial Warden**
  - An enormous ice elemental that reforms after being shattered
  - **Attacks:** Freezes a floor section for 2 seconds, full-room charge, splits into two forms at 50% HP
  - **Strategy:** Torch sword (fire-element weapon) deals bonus damage, must kill both split forms quickly or they recombine
  - **Drop:** Frost Shard (Portal Piece 3) + Glacite Ore (high-defense armor material)

---

### Sanctum 4 — The Marshveil *(Marshland, E)*

A sunken mausoleum half-swallowed by the bog. Fog reduces visibility and the layout is intentionally disorienting. **Landmark:** a ring of pale glowing stones visible through the bog fog.

- **Floor 1 — Reduced visibility:** Fog of war via GBA hardware window feature, torch required to see
- **Floor 2 — Mimics and hazards:** Mimic enemies disguised as chests, poison gas vents on floor tiles
- **Floor 3 — Boss: The Bog Specter**
  - A massive spectral figure that phases in and out of visibility
  - **Attacks:** Turns invisible for 5 seconds then strikes from a random direction, poisons on hit, summons Miasma Clouds that shrink the safe area
  - **Strategy:** Watch for floor ripple telegraphing reappearance position, anti-poison potion essentially mandatory
  - **Drop:** Veil Shard (Portal Piece 4) + Spectral Dust (Alchemy Table upgrade material)

---

### Sanctum 5 — The Emberdepth *(Volcanic, NE)*

A deep forge-temple carved into the volcano by an ancient civilization. Fire resistance potion is essentially mandatory. **Landmark:** a massive glowing volcanic vent surrounded by ancient carved pillars.

- **Floor 1 — Lava tile hazards:** Crossing requires timing or stone bridge building (blocks carried in)
- **Floor 2 — Forge Constructs:** Iron golems that require high damage threshold weapons to defeat
- **Floor 3 — Boss: The Ember Titan**
  - A towering armored construct of ancient iron and living lava
  - **Attacks:** Lava pool creation covering tiles permanently until cooled, stomp shockwaves, ranged lava projectiles
  - **Strategy:** Carry water flasks (craftable) to cool lava tiles and restore safe movement area
  - **Drop:** Ember Shard (Portal Piece 5) + Magma Core (required for Sanctum Alloy armor)

---

### Sanctum 6 — The Hollow Throne *(Corrupted, SE)*

The final Sanctum and the source of the corruption spreading across Hollow Shore. The entrance **only opens when all 5 Portal Pieces are in the player's inventory**. Enemies in this section spawn during the day as well as night. **Landmark:** the entire section glows with a sickly purple light visible from adjacent sections.

- **Requirement:** All 5 Portal Pieces must be held to enter
- **Floor 1 — Corruption zones:** Dark tiles drain health passively, must navigate around or sprint through
- **Floor 2 — Echo enemies:** Corrupted reflections of the player mirroring movements with a delay
- **Floor 3 — Boss: The Hollow Sovereign**
  - The ancient entity that pulled the player to Hollow Shore — the true antagonist
  - **Phase 1:** Summons corrupted versions of all previous boss types in sequence
  - **Phase 2:** Direct combat — reality-warping attacks briefly invert controls, screen-filling corruption waves
  - **Strategy:** Most complex fight in the game, requires full stamina management, food buffs, and best available armor
  - **Drop:** The Hollow Keystone (Portal Piece 6) — combining all 6 pieces at the Alchemy Table completes the Tide Portal

